        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hiwassee, North Carolina; Cherokee County, North Carolina; Swain County, North Carolina; Graham County, North Carolina; North Carolina, United States\n- Systems: Tennessee Valley Authority system\n- Products: Hiwassee Dam; Fontana Dam; Hiwassee Reservoir\n- Places: Hiwassee River; Little Tennessee River\n\nFacts:\n- Fontana Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the Little Tennessee River in Swain and Graham counties, North Carolina, United States.\n- Hiwassee is a small village in Cherokee County, North Carolina.\n- Hiwassee sits next to Hiwassee Dam and the artificially created Hiwassee Reservoir on the Hiwassee River.\n- Hiwassee Dam is 307 feet tall.\n- Hiwassee Dam is the third highest dam in the Tennessee Valley Authority system, behind only Fontana Dam and Watauga Dam.",
